    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:2rem;">Why This Category Matters</h2>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      Bangladesh is the world's second-largest garment exporter with $47 billion in annual exports according to <a href="https://www.bgmea.com.bd" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">BGMEA</a>. The country produces 40% of EU denim imports and supplies major retailers worldwide.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      In our {companyAge} of Bangladesh RMG industry experience, we have seen the transformation from Accord and Alliance reforms to the current era of sustainability compliance. The <a href="https://www.ilo.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">ILO</a> reports Bangladesh has made significant progress in workplace safety since 2013.
    </p>
    <div style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <p style="font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">What is clothing manufacturing?</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">Clothing manufacturing transforms raw materials into finished garments through cutting, sewing, and finishing processes. The process includes pre-production (pattern making, sampling), production planning, cutting, assembly, quality control, and delivery. Bangladesh specialises in knitwear, denim, and woven garments with export-ready factories serving international brands.</p>
    </div>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">
      The global apparel market is projected to reach $2.25 trillion by 2025. Bangladesh clothing manufacturers are positioned for growth through competitive pricing, improving sustainability practices, and duty-free access to EU and UK markets.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

