<!-- What Changed in 2026 -->
<section id="what-changed-2026" style="padding:4rem 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:2rem;">What Changed in Bangladesh Clothing Manufacturing in 2026</h2>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      The Bangladesh garment industry shifted significantly in 2025–2026. New regulations and market dynamics changed how brands must source from Bangladesh.
    </p>
    <div style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <p style="font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Bangladesh LDC Graduation</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">Bangladesh graduates from Least Developed Country status in November 2026. This changes preferential trade agreements and may affect duty structures. Brands sourcing from Bangladesh should evaluate tariff impacts on their pricing models. Duty-free access to EU and UK markets may be affected. Use our <a href="/tools/garment-cost-calculator" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">Garment Cost Calculator</a> to model the cost impact.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <p style="font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">EU Digital Product Passport Preparation</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">GOTS 7.0 certified factories have the traceability infrastructure needed for the 2027 EU Digital Product Passport requirement. Manufacturers without certification systems will need significant investment to comply. Check your EU DPP readiness with our free <a href="/tools/eu-readiness-checker" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">EU Readiness Checker</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <p style="font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">UFLPA Cotton Tracing</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">The Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act requires cotton sourcing documentation. Bangladesh manufacturers must trace cotton origin to avoid UFLPA enforcement. Brands must ensure their Bangladesh suppliers provide cotton origin certificates for US market compliance.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:2rem;">
      <p style="font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">CBAM Carbon Costs</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;">The EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism imposes carbon costs on energy-intensive imports. Bangladesh's coal-dependent electricity may increase costs versus cleaner energy countries. Manufacturers investing in renewable energy gain competitive advantages.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

