        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the difference between FOB and CIF pricing?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">FOB (Free On Board) covers costs up to the port in Bangladesh — you pay freight, insurance, and import duty from there. CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) includes shipping to your destination port. Most Bangladesh manufacturers quote FOB Chittagong or Dhaka. Use our <a href="/tools/garment-cost-calculator" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:none;">Garment Cost Calculator</a> to see your total landed cost under both scenarios.</p>
      </div>
